- **The lease (restored, ADR-0654 D1):** Queues must drain questions whose review date has lapsed;
  the library stores a 7-day lease unless given another. Renew only after reviewing an open
  question's assumptions; the library refuses to renew a settled question.

fields.body:
*Moved from storytree 0.2's library at cutover (2026-09-27), where this increment was `storytree-0-3-own-library-arc-inc-01`. ADR numbers in this text are 0.2's decision numbers; 0.2's copy stays readable there.*

**Stories.** Generalise the seed (`scripts/seed-library-story.mjs` and `scripts/library-seed.mjs` in `C:\code\storytree03`) from the library story alone to every `stories/*.md`. Keep its rules:
- it updates in place and never duplicates;
- it writes only the verified column, from a real test run of that story's tests;
- a story whose tests do not run yet is left "not checked", never "passing".

**Decisions.** Load the 0.3 decisions as front covers through the library's public API: `frontCoverOf`, which ADR-0627 introduced and storytree-ai/storytree#7 landed. Confirm each candidate against the live store before loading it:
- ADR-0621 (the library's tree) on the library story;
- ADR-0627 (knowledge entrances) on the library's capability 9;
- ADR-0626 (the agent link's tree) on the agent-link story;
- ADR-0624 (the read record) on the agent link's activity log and agent tools parts.

A cover covers one node only, so where a decision spans two parts, ask which one it belongs on or split it.

Project-wide decisions (ADR-0617, ADR-0623 and ADR-0625) wait for the owner's answer; see this arc's intent. ADR-0622 (the rename) is 0.2 infrastructure, so leave it out unless the owner says otherwise.

**Practicalities.** The seed stops and starts the app's own Postgres (`~/.storytree/0.3/pgdata`), so it cannot run while the app is open.

**Coordination.** The agent-link session is building `packages/agent-link` and may add story editing to `packages/library` (ADR-0625 D3 story 1). Tell it before you change `scripts/seed*`. Tests follow ADR-0623.

**Landing.** Land through a pull request into storytree-ai/storytree, never squashed, and quote `pnpm test-ratio`'s "all" row in the debrief.

*Moved from storytree 0.2's library at cutover (2026-09-27), where this increment was `0-3-librarian-home`. ADR numbers in this text are 0.2's decision numbers; 0.2's copy stays readable there.*

ADR-0633 D3 item 12 (owner-decided 2026-09-26) brings in 0.3's librarian: 0.2's librarian-curator role, which dedupes, keeps cross-references and keeps the decision log honest. ADR-0631 D2 relies on it to link whole-project decisions to the capability-level ones. Nothing yet decides what it is in 0.3 (an agent role in the library, a tool, or a story of its own). Draft that home and its capability tree, and put them to the owner before code. Work from 0.2's `librarian-curator` agent and its processes.
**Residue (2026-09-27, session modest-mayer-eee9a7, branch claude/modest-mayer-eee9a7).** The home and tree are drafted and put to the owner as `oq-0-3-librarian-capability-tree` (revision 1). There is also a private readable page: https://claude.ai/artifact/Ex8h4djGjae8ac3knyE6Uh (republish from any session with its url). Nothing is built (ADR-0625 D5), and no repo files changed.
- **Recommended home:** H1, a story of its own, "the librarian", reaching the library only through its API.
- **The tree:** six capabilities, each with a shelf of decided, proposed and your-call books:
  1. Links (ADR-0631 D2's links come first);
  2. Decision log;
  3. Catalogue;
  4. Graduation;
  5. Queues;
  6. Rounds.
- **Open choices:**
  - H: its home;
  - U: users' projects (recommended: build for any project, switch on with `0-3-app-users-own-projects`);
  - S: fold 0.2's graduation-synthesist into Queues;
  - R: ranked related / unlinked search, homed in the library's search;
  - G: decision health check as a report, since CI cannot reach a local library.
- **Boundaries:**
  - **Agent link: AGREED by message** with the "Draft the agent link's revised tree (ADR-0633)" session. Its tool server takes tools contributed by another story through one registration point (which also gives them a people's command-line door). `land` returns a "next" line contributors fill, and `land` itself decides nothing about curation. Question raise, settle and retire stay the agent link's.
  - **Library: PROPOSED, and written onto `0-3-library-tree-for-adr-0633`** (the message to the "Drive the 0.3 library lane" session expired unapproved and was never delivered). The library stores status, derived supersession, edges, load-bearing, numbers, kinds, questions and history. It refuses dangling links, supersession loops, and a settle with no answer. It owns the one "current decisions" reading. The librarian holds no data. If that lane's tree decides otherwise, the resuming session matches it in revision 2.
- **To resume:** read the owner's answer on the question. Settle it with an ADR, `storytree question settle … --adr <n> --pg`, in the same landing. Then write `stories/librarian.md` in the 0.3 repo (C:\code\storytree03), with a decision file for its tree.

*Moved from storytree 0.2's library at cutover (2026-09-27), where this increment was `0-3-planet-packed-see-through`. ADR numbers in this text are 0.2's decision numbers; 0.2's copy stays readable there.*

**Build ADR-0648: the globe packs its islands together on a see-through grey ball, with no sea.** The owner decided this on 2026-09-27, from the look test `spike/globe-land` (storytree-ai/storytree), option A.

1. **Packed placement (a new book on Story nodes' shelf, ADR-0648 D1).** Stories take spots on a spiral from the globe's front pole, with neighbouring coasts a few ground units apart, on one fixed globe radius. Each spot comes from its place number alone and never moves (P1). The spike measured radius 160 with 36 frozen places. Carry that over, or compute the spiral from the place number if that can be proven stable, and state the capacity. Places past it are refused. The even-spread book `placeOnGlobe` (#74) gives way: the page stops using it. Retire it, or keep it if other code reads it, and say which.
2. **See-through grey shell (ADR-0648 D2).** Replace lane B's opaque `#101418` sea sphere (#75) with a light, see-through grey surface, so the ball's shape shows, the land visibly covers only part of it, and the far side and the future core show through. L1 light, the islands and the kit trees are unchanged.
3. **The page (#78)** uses both, and keeps names, clicks, claim markers, the opening turn toward a failing island, and the edge markers working.

**Proof, red then green (ADR-0623):**
- the same stories always get the same packed spots;
- adding or retiring a story moves none;
- neighbours' coasts never overlap up to the stated capacity, at the real island sizes;
- a place past capacity is refused;
- the sea sphere is gone and the shell is transparent (a behaviour test on the globe mount's materials).

The look is judged by the owner's eye: bring a headless-Chromium screenshot of 0.3's seeded stories. The laptop session adds `pnpm desktop:smoke`. Update `stories/forest.md` (the books on capabilities 1 and 3), and add `decisions/planet-packed-see-through.md` as 0.3's copy of ADR-0648.

Lands as its own non-draft PR (CI `verify` on three systems, automerged). Quote `pnpm test-ratio`'s "all" row.

*Moved from storytree 0.2's library at cutover (2026-09-27), where this increment was `0-3-planet-knowledge-under-islands`. ADR numbers in this text are 0.2's decision numbers; 0.2's copy stays readable there.*

**Build the library's knowledge beneath each island on the globe, as ADR-0658 decides: K1, faint points only, and loose artifacts pooled at the core.** The owner picked by selecting options on 2026-09-27, after `0-3-planet-knowledge-look`'s pictures (`spike/globe-knowledge`).

Red then green (ADR-0623), for the behaviours:
- every artifact capability 1 places under a shelf is drawn as a faint point beneath the island whose shelf it hangs from, at its computed depth;
- an artifact reached from no shelf is drawn in a small cluster at the globe's centre, never outside the shell;
- nothing is drawn for an artifact capability 1 does not place, and there are no threads;
- islands, names, markers and the V2 pathways are unchanged, and a failing island is never hidden.

Borrow the look test's adapter and capture; never merge the spike. Its front-cover decision file names ADR-0658, a record no other `decisions/*.md` names; the seed refuses a record filed twice. A screenshot comes at landing (`pnpm desktop:smoke` in a throwaway STORYTREE_HOME).
